## Accessing Item Instances

Use `getToolbarItemInstance(key)` to retrieve a toolbar item component instance by its key. The key is either set explicitly in the item definition or derived from the item type when not specified.

The example below registers two custom toolbar items that mirror the [Columns Tool Panel](./tool-panel-columns/) and [Filters Tool Panel](./tool-panel-filters/) toggles. External buttons call `getToolbarItemInstance` to drive each item programmatically.

{% gridExampleRunner title="Accessing Item Instances" name="accessing-instances" /%}

{% apiDocumentation source="grid-api/api.json" section="accessories" names=["getToolbarItemInstance"] /%}

## Theme Parameters

The toolbar exposes the following [Theme Parameters](./theming-parameters/):

| Parameter                | Description                                                                 |
| ------------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `toolbarBackgroundColor` | Background colour of the toolbar. Defaults to the header background colour. |
| `toolbarTextColor`       | Text colour in the toolbar. Defaults to the header text colour.             |
| `toolbarSeparatorBorder` | Border style for the vertical separator between toolbar items.              |
